What are we targeting? Depending on your use case, you may have the need to remove the back button on your events. Sometimes this is useful if you are directing people directly to the ticket selection page and bypassing the events landing page. Here is the back button we are referring to: 
 CSS You can use custom CSS to remove the back button. Below is the CSS you will want to use to accomplish this: 
 .material-icons { display: none !important; } 
 .mat-focus-indicator.back-button.mat-icon-button.mat-button-base { display: none !important; } 

 The end result should look something like this: Additional Resources

What is DocumentLink? Our DocumentLink feature allows you to send invoices to your customers for payment over the web. 
 Main Use Case:  Send customers a DocumentLink URL to view an itemized invoice and pay. 
 Quick Video:  Check out the overview video below to see it in action!  &#128249; 
 Learning Objectives in this Lesson: Learn how to authorize DocumentLink Generate an invoice to send to your customer Quickly create an invoice from an Opportunity 
 Quick Tip:  You can use the "Amount to Pay" field to capture multiple payments against 1 invoice.  &#128184;

What is Paylink? Description:  PayLink is our beautiful, mobile-responsive payment request. For every transaction that's created, a unique link (PayLink) is created. This link can be manually or automatically emailed (or texted!) to your customers for payment.  &#128163; 
 Main Use Case:  Send customers an email or SMS message (Using Blackthorn Messaging) from Salesforce containing a PayLink URL so they can make an immediate payment. 
 Learning Objectives: 1. Learn how to install PayLink from the Payments Setup Wizard.  &#129668; 2. Understand how to provide users with license and permission set access. 3. Quickly configure PayLink to the look and feel of your company.  &#128374;? 
 Quick Tip:  You can create multiple PayLink configurations to change the look and feel of payment requests!  &#129327; 
 Quick Video:  Check out the quick 2-minute video below to see it in action!  &#127909;

What is Paylink? Description:  PayLink is our beautiful, mobile-responsive payment request. For every transaction that's created, a unique link (PayLink) is created. This link can be manually or automatically emailed (or texted!) to your customers for payment.  &#128163; 
